  <div class="fb-content">
    <h2 class="fb-title fb-title--small">Keeping Kids Safe</h2>

    <div class="fb-prose">
      <h2>What is asked for at sign-up</h2>
      <p>A username, an email address and a password. Nothing else. No real name, no address, no phone number, and no date of birth is collected by the site as it is currently built. The email is used to sign in and to recover the account, and it is never shown to another member.</p>
      <p>A sign-up step for members under the age of majority, involving a parent or guardian, is still being designed. It is not drawn on the registration page as a checkbox that does nothing.</p>

      <h2>Who can contact a member</h2>
      <p>Private messages exist between members. A message can be reported, and reporting puts it in front of a moderator. Blocking a member, and the rule that a member cannot be messaged by somebody they have blocked, belong to the social service and are not built yet.</p>

      <h2>Reporting</h2>
      <p>Every profile and message carries a Report Abuse link. Reports land in one moderation queue rather than being sent to an inbox where they might sit unread.</p>

      <h2>How moderation works</h2>
      <p>A moderator can warn an account or restrict it. Restrictions are recorded against the account and checked on every request, so a restricted account cannot avoid them by finding a page that forgot to check. A temporary restriction stops applying when its end date passes and stays in the account's history. Every administrative action is written to a log with the reason and the staff member, and that log cannot be edited from the admin panel.</p>

      <h2>About this page</h2>
      <p>This page describes what the site is built to do. FieldBrik 0.3 is still under construction: accounts, messaging and moderation are the next stage. Where a feature is described in the future tense, it does not exist yet and is not being pretended.</p>
    </div>

    <%- include('../partials/parents-nav') %>
  </div>
